      "before": "a1-u03-d02-e01",
      "title": { "en": "Six to ten" },
      "body": { "en": "*Sześć*, *siedem*, *osiem*, *dziewięć*, *dziesięć*. *Dziewięć* (9) and *dziesięć* (10) are easy to mix up: nine has a *w*, said like English v, and ten has *si*, said like *ś*." }
    },
    {
      "id": "a1-u03-d02-t02",
      "before": "a1-u03-d02-e11",
      "title": { "en": "Ile and numer" },
      "body": { "en": "*Ile* asks \"how many\" or \"how much\": *ile to jest dwa plus sześć?* *Numer* is a number that names something, such as a house, a room or a bus: *numer pięć*." }
    }
